SED Command

SED is a stream editor. It serves the purpose of modifying the texts in the stream according to the given pattern.

AWK Command
awk is mostly used for transforming data files and producing formatted reports
$ awk options 'selection criteria {action}' input file > output file


nano data.csv
ID      Date  Services Status
1 2019-2-10 httpd ok
2 2019-2-10 nginx ok
3 2019-2-10 httpd warning
4 2019-2-10 nginx warning
5 2019-2-10 httpd ok
6 2019-2-10 hginx ok

cat data.csv
awk '{print}' data.csv
   awk '{print$0}' data.csv all the records
awk '/pattern/{print$0}' data.csv all the matches records
   awk '/nginx/{print$0}' data.csv 
   awk '{print NR,$0}' data.csv all the lines rows
awk '{print Nf,$0}' data.csv all the columns
Formatting output with Output Record Separator (ORS)
awk 'BEGIN{ORS="\n\n"}{print $0}' data.csv
awk 'BEGIN{ORS="\n\t"}{print $0}' data.csv
awk 'BEGIN{ORS="\n\n"}{print $0}' data.csv

Formatting output fields with Output Field Separator (OFS)
awk 'BEGIN{OFS="--"}{print $1,$2}' data.csv
awk 'BEGIN{OFS="  "}{print $1,$2}' data.csv
awk 'BEGIN{OFS="sep"}{print $1,$2}' data.csv

